  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef knows the projected sales of his store for the next NNN days. The projected sales of the ithi^{th}ith day is AiA_iAi​.\n\nOn any particular day, Chef can announce that his shop is closing which will **double** his sales for that day, but since Chef is a man of his word, he won't make any sale after that day.\n\nFind the **maximum** possible total sales which Chef can make.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains an integer NNN  — the number of days.\nThe second line consists of NNN space-separated integers denoting the projected sales of each day.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, the **maximum** total sales that Chef can make.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤3⋅1051 \\leq T \\leq 3 \\cdot 10^51≤T≤3⋅105",
      "1≤N≤3⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 3 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤3⋅105",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^91≤Ai​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 3⋅1053 \\cdot 10^53⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n2\n1 2\n3\n7 1 2",
        "output": "5\n14",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Chef announces the closing on second day. Chef can double the sales of the second day to get 1+2⋅2=51 + 2\\cdot2 = 51+2⋅2=5 total sales.\nTest case 222: Chef announces the closing on first day. Chef can double the first day sales but will have no sale on the second and third day. This gives Chef a total sales of 7⋅2=147\\cdot2 = 147⋅2=14."
      }
    ]
  },
